Part of #34. Gives SurveyBeat the small design system SPEC §6 asks for (tokens, typography, about a dozen composed components) and restyles every Release 1 surface with it.

**Direction:** B2 "Conversation, premium" from the design canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/YJbDbUUwgtJeuAshnXrZTh, row 4). Chosen 2026-11-09 over A (Rhythm) and C (Console): one calm column, plain-language results, privacy rules visible in the product, premium enough for B2B buyers.

## Tokens
- Colour: stone ground `#F3F4F1`, surface `#FFFFFF`, line `#E1E5E1`, ink `#0E2A24`, muted text `#3D554F`, primary deep teal `#0B5D55`, dark panel evergreen `#0E2A24` with mint `#9FD6CB` accents, brass `#F6EEDC` / `#6A4F12` only for "bigger change than usual", danger for errors.
- Type: Figtree (UI), Newsreader (page headlines, large scores, section titles). Self-hosted in the app (no third-party font requests); the answer page and emails use system stacks for budget and client support.
- Radius: 20px panels, 12px controls. Touch targets ≥ 44px. WCAG 2.2 AA contrast.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] Tokens defined once in the app's Tailwind `@theme`; the answer page CSS and email theme use the same values, and a test fails when they drift.
- [ ] `components.ts` provides the shared components (page shell and nav, panel, button variants, fields, alert, empty state, badge, table, chart frame with its table view); no screen uses raw Tailwind palette colours.
- [ ] Every app screen restyled: sign-in, Organization creation and choice, Teams, Team, Settings, Pulses and the Pulse editor, Rounds, Results, privacy.
- [ ] Results: per-aggregate line "N people, above your minimum of M" and a "How this page protects people" panel with only true statements (anonymous storage, minimum group size, comment redaction, admins can't see Results unless in the Team).
- [ ] Answer page restyled within ADR 0008's budget (budget test passes, Lighthouse gate passes).
- [ ] Emails restyled, dark mode kept, snapshots updated.
- [ ] Scene and Story tests, e2e axe audit pass.

## Out of scope (follow-ups)
- Generated summary sentence at the top of Results.
- Organization name and initial in the header.
- App dark mode.

